@startuml test-status-flow
title Test status flow (TestStatus), step by step

autonumber "<b>0."
hide footbox
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam MinClassWidth 130
skinparam ParticipantPadding 10
skinparam NoteTextAlignment center
skinparam BoxPadding 10

actor "Author" as author
participant "CREATED" as created
participant "FAILED" as failed #F8D7DA
participant "GENERATED" as generated
participant "REQUIRES_REVIEW" as requiresReview
participant "REVIEWED" as reviewed
participant "PUBLISHED" as published #DDEBF7

== 1. Generation ==

author -> created : POST /api/tests

alt no option flagged
  created -> generated : generation done
else ≥ 1 option flagged
  created -> requiresReview : generation done
else exception
  created -> failed : generation threw
  hnote over failed : end
end

== 2. Review (allowed in GENERATED, REQUIRES_REVIEW, REVIEWED) ==

loop until no question needs review
  author -> requiresReview : review action
  alt a question still needs review
    requiresReview -> requiresReview : stays
  else last flagged question resolved
    requiresReview -> reviewed : resolved
  end
end

alt regenerated question comes back flagged
  generated -> requiresReview : flagged
  reviewed -> requiresReview : flagged
end

note across
  Every review action locks the test row (SELECT … FOR UPDATE) and checks the status under the lock.
end note

== 3. Publish: POST /api/tests/{testId}/publish ==

alt status is GENERATED
  generated -> published : publish
else status is REVIEWED
  reviewed -> published : publish
else status is REQUIRES_REVIEW (or other)
  author -> requiresReview : publish
  requiresReview --> author : 409 Conflict
end

note across
  PUBLISHED: content frozen, accepts attempts, review actions return 409.
end note

== 4. Unpublish: POST /api/tests/{testId}/unpublish ==

alt no attempts, was GENERATED
  published -> generated : unpublish
else no attempts, was REVIEWED
  published -> reviewed : unpublish
else attempts exist
  published --> author : 409 Conflict
end

note across
  Unpublish restores previousStatus from the latest TEST_PUBLISHED event (fallback REVIEWED),
  so review is possible again (step 2).
end note

@enduml
